 "text": "Services | Blue Earth County, MN - Official Website\nSkip to Main Content\n-->\nAbout Us\nCounty Government\nDepartments\nServices\nHow Do I…?\nSearch\nA-Z Services\nAdults & Families\nDay Care\nExtension Services\nSupportive Housing\nHuman Services / Social Services\nVeterans Services\nBirth & Death Records\nElections\nEmergency Management\nEnvironment\nFacility Efficiency & Green Design\nWaste & Recycling\nHorticulture / Agriculture Programs\nLakes, Rivers & Wetlands\nHousing\nLaw, Justice & Public Safety\nAttorney’s Office\nCivil Processing\nCourts\nSheriff’s Office & Jail\nLicense Center\nDriver's Licenses / State ID Card\nBirth and Death Records\nHunting & Fishing Licenses\nMarriage Licenses & Records\nMinnesota REAL IDs\nMotor Vehicle Registrations & Transfers\nNotary Commission Registration\nMinisterial Credentials\nRecreational Vehicle Licenses\nPassports\nProperty Reports & Information\nProperty & Roads\nBuilding, Feedlots & Zoning\nGIS and Property Data Requests\nProperty & Land\nPublic Works / Roads\nServices and Records\nSeptic Systems\nSeptic Compliance Inspections\nSeptic System Disclosure\nSeptic System Funding / Loans\nSeptic System Installation Permits\nSeptic System Operating Permits\nSSTS Ordinance Sec 6-501. SSTS Requiring an Operating Permit\nMaintaining Septic Systems\nSSTS Ordinance Sec 6-419 - Maintenance\nWells\nWell Disclosure\nWell Sealing\nWell Disclosure\nWell & Well Sealing Funding / Loans\nWell Sealing Cost Share Program\nWater Testing\nHealth Services\nCar Seat Safety & Education\nImmunizations\nWomen, Infant & Children (WIC)\nRecording\nRecreation\nArea Activities & Maps\nParks, Trails & Campgrounds\nHome\nServices\nServices\n9\n1\n1\n2\nA-Z Services\nAccess a listing of services available from Blue Earth County.\nAdults & Families\nLearn about programs and services available from the County's Human Services / Social Services and Extension Programs.\nBirth & Death Records\nSubmit requests for various vital records.\nElections\nLearn about where to register to vote, view past election results, and find contact information for current elected officials.\nEmergency Management\nKeep your family safe by being prepared for a disaster or emergency.\nEnvironment\nFind information for area recycling, garbage collection, agriculture programs, as well as area lakes, rivers, and wetlands.\nHousing\nWork with local organizations to help meet housing needs across the area.\nLaw, Justice & Public Safety\nAccess the County's Attorney's Office, Sheriff's Office and Jail, and various courts.\nLicense Center\nQuickly find who to contact for driver's licenses, marriage licenses, and hunting / fishing licenses.\nPassports\nApply for a passport and view application details.\nProperty Reports & Information\nResidents can view property information, maps, and reports.\nProperty & Roads\nView details on property taxes, maps, building / zoning permits, and wells / septic systems.\nHealth Services\nLearn more about Health Services in your community\nRecording\nRecreation\nCheck out all of the various parks and facilities owned by the City of Pueblo.\n-->\nEmployment\nCounty Board\nCounty Library\nParks & Trails\nProperty & Roads\nLicense & Permits\nElections\nOnline Payments\nContact Us\nBlue Earth County\n204 S. 5th Street\nMankato, MN 56001\nStaff Directory\nSubmit a Question or Comment\nData Requests\nData Practices Policy and Exhibits\nData Practices Inventory\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nSite Map\nWebsite Accessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\n[]\nClose ×",
